  "body": "Auction: 34 Shortland Street, City on Wednesday 4 November 2026 at 10:00AM  (will NOT be sold prior)\r\n\r\nLOOK AT THE ZONE.\r\n\r\nRenovators, flippers and buyers who know how to recognise an opportunity this one's worth a closer look.\r\n\r\nThis three-bedroom, one-bathroom brick-and-tile home needs a refresh, but the real attraction lies beyond the front door. With Macleans College zoning and a location close to Bucklands Beach, Half Moon Bay Marina and the ferry, there's plenty here to get you thinking.\r\n\r\nPicture the kitchen you could create, the interior you could transform and the value you might unlock. Whether you're an experienced renovator looking for your next project or a buyer prepared to put in the work to secure a foothold in this sought-after part of Auckland, the opportunity is here to explore.\r\n\r\nYou can't renovate the location, and you can't add a sought-after school zone after you've bought. The rest is up to you.\r\n\r\n\r\n• Three bedrooms, one bathroom\r\n\r\n• Classic brick-and-tile construction\r\n\r\n• Macleans College zone\r\n\r\n• Close to Half Moon Bay Marina, ferry connections and Bucklands Beach\r\n\r\n• 2024 Capital Value: $1,350,000 (not a price guide)\r\n\r\n• Do your sums, bring your builder and come prepared to see the possibilities.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAuction Wednesday 4 November at City Rooms. Not to be sold prior.\r\n\r\nSee interactive features for this property on barfoot.co.nz. Click the \"View office website\" link at the bottom of this page.",
